INFO 8507 :: Page 29 :: 810 PM Ft Monroe Va Jany 5th 65 7 P. M. for Gen Halleck Wash'n . Please have everything called for by Sherman forwarded without delay - He cannot move until the forage and subsistence called for is received . A special messenger from Sherman has just left here with his requisitions sig 8.20 P. M. US Grant Lt Genl via Cairo Jany 5th 840 pm Jany New Orleans Dec 29th 1865 New Orleans Dec 29th Gen Halleck The operations of Gen Dana & Davidson from the Miss & Gen Granger from the Gulf besides the actual damage inflicted upon the enemy have induced the Governor of Alabama & Miss to call out the militia of their states under the belief that <deletion>the</deletion> Selma & Mobile were both threatened . The operations in which Gen Dana is now engaged will probably terminate by the end of this month & Granger as soon as he has secured the large amount of naval stores captured by him will with draw his troops from Pascagoula . The Militia of Alabama will probably return to their homes still more in disposed than they now are to respond to another call . If Gen Thomas should now be able to carry out the intentions of Gen Sherman in relation to Selma I can be of material service by operations from the river & gulf I will communicate with Gen Thomas & be prepared to aid him as far as possible Ed R. S. Canby M Genl
