INFO 8509 :: Page 31 :: 610 PM Ft. Monroe Jan 6. 1865 230 PM for Bvt Br Gen DC McCallum supt mily RRds Wash the Secy War directs that you proceed without delay to report in person to Gen Sherman at Savannah or wherever he may be found. E. D. Townsend AAG 6 PM NY Jan 6. 1865 NY 6th for QmGen Washn ---- Steamers Surro - Nada & Ashland started last Evening for Balto ---- the Oriental will start early in the morning for same place ---- this will complete the transptn required for the 5.000 troops & 1.000 laborers at Balt sig S VanVliet QM & Br Gen 4 PM 1030 PM Ft Monroe Jany 6th 65 630 P. M. for C. A. Dana Washn . We arrived here safely this after noon and will remain until tomorrow forenoon . I forgot to mention to you that , I shall continue acting as Secretary , issuing orders and making regulations , Your Official style and Signature will be that of your commission , Assistant Secretary , and not acting Secretary . I noticed in my former absence that the latter style had been adopted . But there can be only one acting Acting Secretary and as I shall act ? the style of acting Secretary , proper in some cases , is not in the present case EM Stanton
INFO 8510 :: Page 32 :: 920 AM Ft Monroe Va Jany 7th 65 9 AM for CA Dana Washn I require permission from the War Dept to go on the expedition . A steamer sails immy Please telegraph permit & oblige Tribune Elias Smith Army Correspondent 1030 AM 9 PM Maj Eckert Louisville Ky Jany 6th 1865 Guerrillas under the notorious Magruder cut our telegraph today at Bards town Junction and about time we had that repaired they cut it again at Lebanon Junction and killed four soldiers in Cold blood this cut throat gang of twenty or thirty men has infested that section all Summer murdering every union soldier they find and no effort seems to be made to drive them out or exterminate them snowing hard tonight Sam Bruch
INFO 8511 :: Page 33 :: 12.40 P. M Winchester Jany 7th 1865 To Secy of War The Transports were not ready at Baltimore for Genl Grover and he had to go in to camp this is unfortunate PH Sheridan Maj Genl 730 P. M. Balto Jan 7. 1865. 6 PM for QrMrGen Your dispatch rec'd neither the Surro Nada , Ashland or Oriental have arrived here & I know nothing of their capacity --- The Ariel , Illinois , Victor & Genl Sedgwick now here can carry three thousand men & one hundred horses ---- transportation is required for five thousand soldiers two hundred & thirty horses & for one thousand men of the Construction Corps Expected from the west ---- the Baltic left for Ft. Monroe last night Sig R. M. Newport Col. & Q. M. 9.20 A. M. Jan 8. 1865 Ft. Monroe Va Jan 7. 1865 8 P. M. for Sec Navy ---- The main Journal in 12 hours run shows new cracks , some of them serious . Chf Engineer Robie & Mr Cosgrove contractors Engineer think that from the edges of these cracks reaming away the brass bearings , there will be danger of a break down in going to Wilmington Jno Rodgers
